  "id": "cockayne-syndrome",
  "term": "Cockayne syndrome",
  "definition": "Cockayne syndrome is a genetic disorder involving multiple body systems, marked by short stature, sensitivity to sunlight, early-aging features, and hearing loss. It results from autosomal recessive gene changes affecting transcription-coupled DNA repair, and it is grouped into types based on how severe it is and when it begins.",
